---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import SiteHeader from "../components/SiteHeader.astro";
import SiteFooter from "../components/SiteFooter.astro";
import Section from "../components/ui/Section.astro";
import Button from "../components/ui/Button.astro";
import "../styles/guides.css";
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy | Airdraft"
  description="How Airdraft handles dictation data and optional website analytics, and how to change your analytics choice."
>
  <SiteHeader />
  <main id="main" class="island subpage">
    <Section
      level={1}
      first
      title="Privacy"
      intro="Your dictation and your visit to this website are separate."
    >
      <article
        class="guide-article privacy-article"
        aria-label="Privacy details"
      >
        <h2>Dictation on your Mac</h2>
        <p>
          Local speech and refinement models process dictation on your Mac.
          Cloud speech providers receive your audio. Cloud refinement providers
          receive your transcript and any context you enable. Your provider keys
          are stored in the macOS Keychain.
        </p>
        <p>
          This website analytics integration does not collect data from the
          Airdraft Mac app. The website's interactive samples use authored text
          and never record your microphone.
        </p>
        <h2>Optional website analytics</h2>
        <p>
          When website analytics are enabled, we ask before loading PostHog. If
          you allow it, PostHog receives page visits, selected button actions,
          browser and device type, performance measurements, referral domains
          and campaign labels. A random browser identifier connects those events
          across visits.
        </p>
        <p>
          We do not enable session recordings, capture typed text or create
          identified person profiles. We remove URL queries and fragments,
          referral paths, advertising click identifiers and unrecognized event
          properties before sending events. Campaign labels must not contain
          personal information. We configure PostHog to discard IP addresses and
          disable location enrichment; the service still receives the network
          connection.
        </p>
        <p>
          PostHog uses browser storage after you allow analytics. We also store
          your allow or decline choice on this browser for 180 days. Declining
          sends no website analytics to PostHog. Turning analytics off stops
          future collection and clears the SDK's stored analytics state; it does
          not delete events already received.
        </p>
        <p>
          We honor Global Privacy Control and Do Not Track signals by keeping
          analytics off. Analytics choices apply to this website and browser
          only. JavaScript must be enabled to change the choice or collect
          analytics.
        </p>
        <p>
          Cloudflare hosts the website and handles network requests and access
          controls separately. Following GitHub or payment links takes you to
          those services, under their own privacy practices.
        </p>
        <p>
          Read{" "}
          <a href="https://posthog.com/privacy">PostHog's privacy notice</a> for
          its service practices.
        </p>
        <h2 id="analytics">Your analytics choice</h2>
        <p class="analytics-status" data-analytics-status aria-live="polite">
          Website analytics are off unless you allow them with JavaScript
          enabled.
        </p>
        <div class="analytics-actions analytics-settings">
          <Button data-analytics-choice="denied">Turn Analytics Off</Button>
          <Button data-analytics-choice="granted">Allow Analytics</Button>
        </div>
      </article>
    </Section>
  </main>
  <SiteFooter />
</Layout>
